item.description:
Preview Feature — Requires --enable-preview at compile and runtime. The API stabilized significantly from Java 21 through 24 and will be finalized in a future release.
The Unstructured Concurrency Problem When you submit tasks to an ExecutorService, the tasks are logically related but structurally unconnected — the executor doesn&rsquo;t know they belong together:
// Unstructured concurrency — looks simple, hides serious problems ExecutorService executor = Executors.newCachedThreadPool(); Future&lt;Order&gt; orderFuture = executor.

Preview Feature — Requires --enable-preview at compile and runtime.
The Boilerplate Problem Teaching Java to a beginner means explaining class declarations, access modifiers, static, and String[] before they can print &ldquo;Hello, World!&rdquo;:
// Traditional Java — 4 concepts before printing one line public class HelloWorld { public static void main(String[] args) { System.out.println(&#34;Hello, World!&#34;); } } Every word carries meaning, but that meaning is irrelevant until the student understands OOP, the JVM class model, and program entry points.
